title: Mussolini appointed Prime Minister!
subtitle: Our nightmare has come true.
view-if: march_succeeded = 1 and pnf_leader = "Mussolini"
tags: event
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: ul_in_government = 1; ds_in_government = 1; pnf_in_government = 1; ppi_in_government = 1 if ppi_relation < 78; ppi_in_government = 0 if ppi_relation > 78
face-image: img/mussolini_power.jpeg


= Mussolini Appointed Prime Minister!

After the March on Rome, [+ king +] has appointed Mussolini to the position of Prime Minister, with many fearing he will start to consolidate power and bring a <span style="color: [+ pnf_colour +];">fascist</span> dictatorship to our country, as <span style="color: [+ pnf_colour +];">fascists</span> take over ministries and begin cracking down on the Red Guard and other leftist groups.  

Mussolini has formed a coalition between the UL, DS, PNF, [? if ppi_in_government = 0 : and the ?] ANI [? if ppi_in_government = 1 : and the PPI ?]  in order to maintain power. [? if ppi_in_government = 0 : However, surprisingly, the PPI has refused to join the coalition due to their good relations with us. ?]

What are we to do now?

- @fight: We must not allow him to consolidate power; mobilize the Red Guard!
- @keep_on: Await our opportunity to strike.


@fight

Do we realize that this means civil war, against the full force of the state?

- @civil_war: Yes.
- @keep_on: We are not ready for war. Instead, we will continue to struggle and await our opportunity.

@keep_on
subtitle: The game is not over.
